A||||1||Rex||Tach Filter????||||1||
Z||000000||Rex||05-17-2001||07:18 PM||||OK I've read up on here about a tach filter<BR>being bad and some of it's symptoms.<BR>Some of the info offsets others. My simple question is if ( tach filter ) is bad will it cause the engine to misfire? Also to check it can it be unplugged and a shunt or bridge wire put across the plug? Thanks for your help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||05-18-2001||09:10 AM||||All you have to do to check it is unplug it and see if your symptoms go away. Don't use a jumper wire across the terminals to check it.<P>The tach filter "smooths" the inputs to the tach...putting a jumper wire in its place could result in damage to the tach.<P>I've had "jumpy tach" syndrome that was caused by water in the distributor cap...if this is what you're experiencing, take the cap off and check for this. Also be sure the metal "can" of the tach filter is grounded to the engine block.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
